---
import WysFrame from '../../components/WysFrame.astro';
import WysPhoto from '../../components/WysPhoto.astro';
import {WYS_ROOT,examples,contents,imageNotice} from '../../data/wys.js';
const steps=[{n:'01',title:'Choose your look',text:'Start with a theme and your approved product inputs.'},{n:'02',title:'Prepare the three views',text:'A basic flat lay, a styled scene and a separately composed lifestyle view.'},{n:'03',title:'Build the destination',text:'Use your eligible Idea List or owned website path. Verify the destination before scheduling.'},{n:'04',title:'Review the finished Pin',text:'Check the image, copy, public board, disclosure, destination and alt text.'},{n:'05',title:'Authorize and track',text:'Choose each exact finished Pin and authorize its schedule. Record the status the publisher confirms.'}];
const faqs=[{q:'Will Pins publish without my approval?',a:'No. Each Pin stays a draft until you select that exact finished Pin and authorize its schedule after checking the image, destination, public board, disclosure, title and alt text.'},{q:'Does my computer have to stay on?',a:'That depends on the execution mode available to your account. Supported Cloud runs may work with your computer off. Local runs require your computer and any needed local session. Your setup needs its own test.'},{q:'What if I do not have an AI persona?',a:'A no-persona path needs a deliberately validated third-image variant. The Tommy Kate examples show the persona path; they do not demonstrate every customer path.'},{q:'Can I use it as an Associate without Influencer approval?',a:'The Associates-only path uses a page on your own site as the destination. Influencer approval is required for the Idea List path. Site writing and publishing depend on your platform and connected actions.'},{q:'Is automatic product finding ready?',a:'No. It needs eligible Amazon Creators API access and a tested connection. Eligibility does not prove that a connection works.'},{q:'Can I buy it now?',a:'The customer product is on hold. Checkout is closed, and the planning dates do not announce a release. You can explore the approved styling examples and follow TDIE updates.'}];
---
<WysFrame title="The While-You-Sleep Storefront™ | The Digital Income Edit" description="Explore TDIE’s guided Amazon-to-Pinterest preparation workflow and approved three-image styling examples. The customer product remains on hold." ogImage={examples[0].photos[2].src.src}>
 <header class="wys-hero wys-wrap">
  <div class="wys-hero-copy"><p class="wys-ribbon">The While-You-Sleep Storefront™</p><h1>Pretty ideas.<br/>A process that <em>pulls its weight.</em></h1><p class="wys-lede">A guided kit for turning your approved Amazon products into Pinterest Pin drafts, with images and copy prepared for your review. Less rebuilding the same routine. More room for the rest of your life.</p><div class="wys-actions"><a class="wys-button" href={WYS_ROOT+'/look-inside'}>Take a look inside <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="wys-text-link" href="#how-it-works">See the process <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div><div class="wys-small-note"><span class="wys-status">Customer product on hold</span><p>You choose each finished Pin and authorize its schedule. Checkout stays closed.</p></div></div>
  <div class="wys-hero-art"><WysPhoto photo={examples[0].photos[2]} treatment="scallop" caption="Pretty Wicked · a real example from the TDIE styling edit" eager/><span class="wys-pearl-badge">Made for<br/><strong>your kind<br/>of pretty.</strong></span></div>
 </header>
 <div class="wys-ticker" aria-label="Workflow principles"><div class="wys-wrap"><span>Approved product inputs</span><span aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span>Three distinct views</span><span aria-hidden="true">✦</span><span>Your review, your schedule</span></div></div>
 <section class="wys-section wys-wrap" aria-labelledby="wys-three-title"><div class="wys-section-head"><div><p class="wys-label">One look, three perspectives</p><h2 id="wys-three-title">From a little collection<br/>to <em>a whole scene.</em></h2></div><p>The same styling idea, carried through a complete flat lay, a styled corner and a natural everyday moment.</p></div><div class="wys-three">{examples[1].photos.map((photo,i)=><div class="wys-role"><span class="wys-role-tab">0{i+1} · {photo.role}</span><WysPhoto photo={photo} treatment={['pink','lavender','double'][i]} /><a class="wys-text-link" href={WYS_ROOT+'/look-inside#ghoul-fuel-coffee-bar'}>Explore this view <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div>)}</div><p class="wys-image-notice">{imageNotice}</p></section>
 <section class="wys-banded" id="how-it-works"><div class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wys-section-head"><div><p class="wys-ribbon wys-ribbon-lavender">A rhythm you can understand</p><h2>Less starting over.<br/><em>More knowing what comes next.</em></h2></div><p>Preparation, review and scheduling are separate steps. The workflow helps you organize them in the right order.</p></div><ol class="wys-process">{steps.map(step=><li><span class="wys-number">{step.n}</span><div><h3>{step.title}</h3><p>{step.text}</p></div></li>)}</ol></div></section>
 <section class="wys-section wys-wrap wys-split" aria-labelledby="wys-real-title"><div class="wys-story-photo"><WysPhoto photo={examples[0].photos[1]} treatment="arch" label="The styled scene"/><span class="wys-paper-tag">From the TDIE edit</span></div><div class="wys-note-sheet"><p class="wys-label">See the actual examples</p><h2 id="wys-real-title">The pretty part has<br/><em>a process behind it.</em></h2><p>These photographs are approved examples from Jodie’s own styling workflow. Open the look, see the three views and read what was selected.</p><p>They are styling inspiration, not exact retail photographs or proof that every customer automation path has passed a live test.</p><a class="wys-button" href={WYS_ROOT+'/look-inside'}>Open the examples <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="wys-text-link" href="/lifestyle/pretty-wicked-entryway">Read Pretty Wicked <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div></section>
 <section class="wys-kit-band"><div class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wys-section-head"><div><p class="wys-label">What the kit is designed to contain</p><h2>A place for every<br/><em>piece of the routine.</em></h2></div><p>Guides, setup and recurring prompts. Availability depends on your accounts and connected capabilities; the customer release remains on hold.</p></div><div class="wys-kit-grid">{contents.map(item=><article class="wys-kit-item"><span class="wys-file-tab">{item.n} / THE KIT</span><h3>{item.title}</h3><p>{item.text}</p></article>)}</div><div class="wys-callout"><strong>Before you buy</strong><p>You need the relevant Amazon account access, a Pinterest business account and a verifiable public board. Image generation, execution and publishing depend on the providers and connections available in your account. No automatic sourcing or unattended publishing is promised.</p></div></div></section>
 <section class="wys-section wys-wrap wys-faq-section" aria-labelledby="wys-faq-title"><div><p class="wys-ribbon">The honest details</p><h2 id="wys-faq-title">Pretty, with<br/><em>the details spelled out.</em></h2><WysPhoto photo={examples[1].photos[0]} treatment="polaroid" caption="Ghoul Fuel · the selected pieces"/></div><div class="wys-faqs">{faqs.map(faq=><details class="wys-faq"><summary>{faq.q}</summary><p>{faq.a}</p></details>)}</div></section>
 <section class="wys-wrap wys-section"><div class="wys-invitation"><div><p class="wys-label">Stay close to the next chapter</p><h2>A little less busy.<br/><em>A little more you.</em></h2><p>The customer product is on hold. Follow TDIE updates while the remaining setup and release checks are completed.</p><a class="wys-button" href={WYS_ROOT+'/waitlist'}>Stay in the loop <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><WysPhoto photo={examples[1].photos[2]} treatment="lavender" caption="Ghoul Fuel · a natural everyday moment"/></div></section>
</WysFrame>
